  "ada/conditional-information.md": "# What the omitted determinant measures

New joint derivation following joint19. This sharpens joint15/16, rather than superseding them. Inherited constructions: branches/branch-3/emmy/rank-m-bridge.md:13-30 and branch-3 ledger75 establish the full determinant cycle; branches/branch-2/ada/common-core-marginal.md:5-24 and branch-2 ledger54 supply Gaussian marginalisation. Joint15/16 combine them and give the sign-reversal witness. These are shared mathematical inputs, not independent molecular validation. No novelty claim is made for the information identities.

Q's target is the bound-minus-aqueous binding quartet (branches/branch-3/inputs/Q.txt:398-428, Eq4/5). P proposes inverse-Hessian displacement correlations (branches/branch-3/ada/P-covariance-primary.txt:40-95, S8.4, an inherited primary-PDF extraction). Neither equates the following auxiliary information with chemical binding nonadditivity. The new result clarifies what is lost when using a common-coordinate determinant as a surrogate.

## Identity

Use the fixed SPD internal-coordinate baseline and positive spring updates of joint15. Partition displacement coordinates into retained and omitted parts:

\[
q=(z,w),\quad K=\begin{pmatrix}A&B\\B^T&D\end{pmatrix},\quad
U=\begin{pmatrix}U_z\\U_w\end{pmatrix},\quad
V=\begin{pmatrix}V_z\\V_w\end{pmatrix}.
\]

Let \(q\) have covariance \(\theta K^{-1}\), and define noisy auxiliary contacts

\[
x=U^Tq+\epsilon_X,\quad y=V^Tq+\epsilon_R,\quad
\operatorname{Cov}(\epsilon_X)=\theta I/a,\quad
\operatorname{Cov}(\epsilon_R)=\theta I/b,\quad \theta=k_BT.
\]

Both noises are independent of each other and of displacement. They implement prescribed spring coefficients, not an observed molecular noise model. The Gaussian conditional distribution has

\[
\operatorname{Cov}(w\mid z)=\theta D^{-1}.
\]

The conditional contact covariance, independent of the value of \(z\), is therefore

\[
\Sigma_{xy\mid z}=\theta\begin{pmatrix}
U_w^TD^{-1}U_w+I/a&U_w^TD^{-1}V_w\\
V_w^TD^{-1}U_w&V_w^TD^{-1}V_w+I/b
\end{pmatrix}.
\]

Apply joint15's determinant/information identity to the omitted blocks \(D_{ij}\), whose updates are exactly \(aU_wU_w^T\) and \(bV_wV_w^T\). For a corner quantity define \(\mathcal C L=L_{11}+L_{00}-L_{10}-L_{01}\). It follows that

\[
\frac12\mathcal C\log\det D=-I(x;y\mid z).
\]

Writing \(S_{ij}=A_{ij}-B_{ij}D_{ij}^{-1}B_{ij}^T\) and using \(\det K_{ij}=\det D_{ij}\det S_{ij}\) gives

\[
\underbrace{\frac12\mathcal C\log\det S}_{\Delta F_{\mathrm{ret}}/\theta}
=I(x;y\mid z)-I(x;y).
\]

This is the negative of the usual interaction-information combination, with its sign convention stated explicitly. Conditioning is not guaranteed to decrease mutual information, so the retained cycle has no universal sign. No dynamical evolution or causal inference is involved.

## Executable evidence

ada/check_conditional_information.py:17-52 checks this in two independent algebraic ways: the conditional contact covariance from \(D^{-1}\), and the conditional covariance from the joint covariance of retained coordinates and contacts. Full, omitted and Schur determinant quartets are evaluated separately.

The joint16 witness gives \(I(x;y)=0.02041099726\) and \(I(x;y\mid z)=0.05889151783\) nats; their difference is the retained cycle \(+0.03848052057\) in thermal units. The omitted cycle is \(-0.05889151783\), restoring the full \(-0.02041099726\). A control with only one bundle acting in omitted coordinates has zero conditional information and retains the full negative cycle. A seeded set of 120 synthetic SPD models with rank-two/rank-three updates verifies all three identities to a maximum residual of \(4.00\times10^{-15}\). These checks cover the algebra, not physical accuracy or general numerical conditioning.

