  "emmy/marginal-bounds.md": "# A conditional correction for common-coordinate stiffness cycles

This is new joint algebra following joint16/20, not new molecular evidence or a novelty claim. Sources are Ada's exact Schur decomposition, ada/information-marginalisation.md:34-63 (joint16), branches/branch-2/ada/common-core-marginal.md:5-24 (branch-2 ledger54), and the prescribed positive-bundle bound in branches/branch-3/emmy/rank-m-bridge.md:13-45 (branch-3 ledger75/86). Joint19 independently proposes the conditional-information interpretation. This note derives the determinant and representation consequences without assuming that interpretation has been checked.

## Fixed-space assumptions and exact bundle reduction

Work on the same SPD internal coordinate space at every corner, with temperature \(\theta=k_BT\). All minima, offsets, configurational measures and kinetic terms are fixed. Partition retained coordinates \(x\) from omitted coordinates \(z\), and write

\[
K=\begin{pmatrix}A&B\\B^T&D\end{pmatrix},\qquad S=A-BD^{-1}B^T.
\]

The four Hessians are \(K_{ij}=K+iUU^T+jVV^T\). Spring coefficients are absorbed into the bundle columns. For a joint bundle \(W=[U,V]\), partition \(W=[W_x^T,W_z^T]^T\). The exact Schur update is

\[
S'=S+L(I+W_z^TD^{-1}W_z)^{-1}L^T,
\qquad L=W_x-BD^{-1}W_z.
\]

Completing the square in \(z\) gives this formula; it is also a block Woodbury identity. It generalises Ada's single-column formula at ada/information-marginalisation.md:47-52. Independent bundles are generally mixed by the small inverse, so additive full Hessian updates need not stay additive after marginalisation.

There is a weaker sufficient preservation condition than requiring both bundles to be wholly retained. If \(V_z=0\), then

\[
S_{10}=S+L_U(I+U_z^TD^{-1}U_z)^{-1}L_U^T,
\quad S_{01}=S+V_xV_x^T,
\quad S_{11}=S_{10}+V_xV_x^T.
\]

Thus one can use an effective positive X bundle \(\widetilde U=L_U(I+U_z^TD^{-1}U_z)^{-1/2}\) and the original retained R bundle. The omitted determinant cycle vanishes, and the full stiffness cycle equals the retained cycle. Merely omitting an extra X nitrogen is not sufficient to break the representation; both substitutions must be checked against the omitted-coordinate map. This is a sufficient condition, not a necessary one. No actual chemical map is supplied by this algebra.

After reading joint21/22/27, the general formula supplies a stronger preservation criterion. If \(U_z^TD^{-1}V_z=0\), the joint inverse in the Schur update is block diagonal, so the reduced quartet is exactly additive in the two effective bundles even when both touch omitted coordinates. The omitted cycle also vanishes. This strengthens the qualification at ada/conditional-information.md:65: under the stated fixed SPD additive model, exact zero conditional cross-compliance does establish retained additivity. A merely small conditional information does not establish an exact additive representation, and none of these conditions validates chemical replacements.

## Omitted response supplies the missing determinant correction

Define the thermal stiffness cycle of any quartet \(J\) by

\[
f(J)=\tfrac12\log\frac{\det J_{11}\det J_{00}}{\det J_{10}\det J_{01}}.
\]

The exact identity is \(f(K)=f(S)+f(D)\), where
\(D_{ij}=D+iU_zU_z^T+jV_zV_z^T\). These omitted blocks remain additive positive updates even when the Schur quartet is non-additive. Consequently

\[
f(D)\le0,\qquad f(K)\le\min\{0,f(S)\}.
\]

Compute \(P_z=U_z^TD^{-1}U_z\), \(Q_z=V_z^TD^{-1}V_z\), and \(R_z=U_z^TD^{-1}V_z\). The inherited determinant lemma gives the exact finite correction from these small blocks. If the supported whitened overlap has singular values \(s_j<1\), its saturation value

\[
\ell_D=\tfrac12\sum_j\log(1-s_j^2)
\]

supplies \(f(S)+\ell_D\le f(K)\le\min\{0,f(S)\}\). A shared supported direction makes this uniform lower bound divergent. Finite known bundle strengths still permit an exact finite correction. These statements concern the full fixed-space stiffness cycle, not Q binding NA.

Importantly, \(\theta D^{-1}\) is the covariance of omitted coordinates conditional on retained coordinates. It is not their marginal covariance \(\theta[K^{-1}]_{zz}\). Ordinary omitted-coordinate covariance therefore does not automatically measure the correction. Full baseline projected solves can provide the required response, or the physically defined omitted block can be solved directly. A repaired P inverse estimator would target the same matrix with its actual conditioning and precision costs; no improved quantum complexity is proved here.

## No retained-data-only finite lower bound

The omitted-response requirement cannot be bypassed with arbitrarily precise retained covariances. Take \(K=I_2\), \(UU^T=\operatorname{diag}(1,t)\), \(VV^T=\operatorname{diag}(4,t)\), \(t\ge0\), retaining coordinate 1. The retained covariance quartet is always \((1,1/2,1/5,1/6)\), its cycle is \(\tfrac12\log(3/5)\), and its additive positive model is exact. Nevertheless

\[
f(K)=\tfrac12\log(3/5)+\tfrac12\log\frac{1+2t}{(1+t)^2}\longrightarrow-\infty.
\]

Both bundles remain positive and all corners remain SPD. This strengthens the general unmeasured-mode witness in branches/branch-3/ledger.jsonl entry12 by keeping additive positive full-space updates and an exactly additive retained quartet. It is an identifiability counterexample, not evidence of hidden thrombin modes. It shows that a successful reduced additive fit does not itself establish absence of hidden contributions.

## Executable checks and practical consequence

emmy/check_marginal_bounds.py verifies the bundle Schur formula, one-omitted-bundle preservation and finite/saturation inequalities in 24 seeded synthetic SPD cases, plus the invisible omitted-mode construction at five strengths. emmy/marginal-bounds-results.json records all values. Largest Schur error is \(1.07\times10^{-14}\); one-bundle additive and cycle errors are at most \(3.56\times10^{-15}\) and \(2.23\times10^{-15}\). These are floating-point corroborations of the derivation, not interval certificates or statistical samples.

An additional control constructs two nonzero omitted bundles orthogonal in the conditional metric and checks both exact reduced additivity and cycle equality in those same 24 cases. Ada's conditional-information derivation at ada/conditional-information.md:17-50 and code at ada/check_conditional_information.py:18-49 were cross-checked by inspection: conditioning the joint covariance indeed produces the omitted response plus independent contact noise, and the three determinant identities follow. This is an independent reasoning check of shared constructions, not a rerun of Ada's script or independent molecular evidence.

