For Q/P, compare the chemical maps before rejecting or accepting the spring representation: determine which substitution bundles touch omitted coordinates, then compute or bound the conditional omitted response when both do. This sharpens the classical prerequisite to P's static covariance readout, branches/branch-3/ada/P-covariance-primary.txt:40-98, whose manuscript normalisation and valid-state issues remain inherited objections. Q Eq4/5, branches/branch-3/inputs/Q.txt:398-428, still requires bound and aqueous free-energy legs. Neither these bounds nor a validated reduced covariance can identify those legs, offsets or basin populations. No F mechanism, binding NA bound, publication novelty or quantum advantage follows.
